id: pm-ts-starter-ho5h
title: Enforce a real coverage gate by running tests against TypeScript sources
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T23:32:41.931Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T23:33:06.017Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T23:33:06.017Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Tests import TypeScript sources rather than dist so coverage reports on editable lines; the gate fails the build when any threshold regresses; the gate fails when a source file never loads, proven by a negative control; thresholds are recorded in package.json as a ratchet at the measured baseline; the gate runs in the release check and in CI on Node 22 and 26"
resolution: "Tests moved onto TypeScript sources and scripts/coverage-gate.ts wired into release:check and CI."
expected_result: "A coverage gate runs in the release check and in CI on both supported Node lines, reports against TypeScript sources, and fails when a source file is untested or a threshold regresses."
actual_result: "npm run check passes. npm run coverage passes with 45 tests, the single source file (index.ts) present in the report, at 89.97 line, 67.47 branch and 74.36 function coverage. A negative control adding an untested __probe.ts (added to the sources list for a flat layout) made the gate exit 1 and name that file, so the presence check is not vacuous. Thresholds pinned at 89/67/74. The flat-layout source previously resolved manifest.json/package.json via ../ relative to dist; readRootJson now resolves them from both dist and source-root locations so the version/SDK-target reads work when run as a source .ts. The Node 22 and 26 CI legs are unobserved until the pull request runs."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:32:50.647Z",pi-agent,"Negative control run: adding an untested __probe.ts to the sources list made the gate exit 1 and name the file,so the presence check is not vacuous."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:32:50.647Z",pi-agent,The flat-layout source index.ts resolved manifest.json/package.json via ../<file> assuming it ran from dist; running it as a source .ts from the repo root resolved above the repo and fell back to 0.0.0/unknown. readRootJson tries the parent (dist location) then the current directory so both layouts resolve the repo-root file.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:32:50.647Z",pi-agent,"Node omits never-loaded files from its coverage report rather than reporting them at zero,so a threshold flag alone is satisfiable by narrowing what the suite imports. Any coverage gate must reconcile the report against the source tree."
files[5]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/coverage-gate.ts,project,coverage gate with source-presence reconciliation
  package.json,project,"coverageGate config and coverage script wired into release:check"
  tsconfig.json,project,rewriteRelativeImportExtensions so sources import siblings as .ts
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project,coverage gate on a Node 22 and 26 matrix
  index.ts,project,readRootJson resolves repo-root json from both dist and source-root locations
tests[2]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  npm run coverage,project,1800
  "npm run release:check",project,3600
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/coverage-gate.ts,project,gate implementation and rationale
close_reason: Coverage gate landed and locally verified; the Node 22 and 26 CI legs are unobserved until the pull request runs.
body: "Baseline measured 2026-07-29 across one source file (index.ts): 89.97 line, 67.47 branch, 74.36 function coverage. Thresholds are pinned at the measured floor (89/67/74) so the number can only move up."
